                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "715cbbc5-5ef4-383c-9b10-fe8a3668d71b",
                                        "entry_id": "8044da6c-5d5e-388c-bc8a-c852f08b9221",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The daughter of Zeus and Leda, considered to be the most beautiful woman in the world; her abduction by Paris brought about the Trojan War."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Greek",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7a904bd-46b6-4ecb-ae2f-2e6fd4f16c36",
                                                "sense_id": "715cbbc5-5ef4-383c-9b10-fe8a3668d71b",
                                                "text": "Fools on both sides! Helen must needs be fair,\nWhen with your blood you daily paint her thus."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "56671f3c-639d-3408-ad73-31e874942dab",
                                        "entry_id": "8044da6c-5d5e-388c-bc8a-c852f08b9221",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female given name from Ancient Greek."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2196e0d-a9c7-4e88-baed-9f49342364af",
                                                "sense_id": "56671f3c-639d-3408-ad73-31e874942dab",
                                                "text": "\"Is her name Ellen or Helen, Miss Viner? I thought —\"\nMiss Viner closed her eyes.\n\"I can sound my h's, dear, as well as anyone, but Helen is not a suitable name for a servant. I don't know what the mothers in the lower classes are coming to nowadays.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e8e6675-479f-4cfe-8308-30c3f5fb843c",
                                                "sense_id": "56671f3c-639d-3408-ad73-31e874942dab",
                                                "text": "...in 1910 she brought Helen into the world, the little female, or \"mujercita\", as her mother called all the babies, naming her after the glittery label on a facial ointment, The Helen of Troy Beauty Pomade, said to eradicate wrinkles, to soften and add a youthful glow to the user's skin - a fortuitous choice because, of all the sisters, she would be the most beautiful and, never growing old, would always possess the face of a winsome adolescent beauty."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a6f6e1a-1c97-4fc8-aeb6-7064e1fabc47",
                                                "sense_id": "56671f3c-639d-3408-ad73-31e874942dab",
                                                "text": "Gemma followed her, thinking that Helen seemed rather an old-fashioned and elegant name for this rumpled young mother."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3f83abfb-0185-3e25-b1ab-dd580061b05b",
